{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932101-dramatic-combat-failures","id":932101,"title":"Dramatic Combat Failures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-15T11:03:08-07:00","id":932101,"title":"Dramatic Combat Failures","content":"Hey all, <br /> <br /> Just wanted to throw out a quick question. I've got a player who's taking Thief of Fate and I'm seriously considering recommending &quot;Unarmed Defence&quot; for her. It seems like a really fun way of beefing up her combat utility. The tl;dr, for those without the book to hand, is that anyone who touches a Thief of Fate upgrades failures to dramatic failures for the next 24 hours. Unarmed Defence boosts your defence while not dodging and rewards you for causing your opponents attack rolls to fail. Together, you've got someone who is good at not being hit, and punishes people who miss her (Armed Defence might also work). <br /> <br /> However, I'm just not sure on how potent dramatic failures should be in combat. For the PCs its easy, because there's lots of little things you can do to cause them problems later. Maybe their clothes tear or their face bruises, and they have to explain what happened. Maybe they lose their phone in the fight, either inconveniencing them, or letting their opponent ID them. <br /> <br /> But when they're up against NPCs, the dramatic failures should be more immediate, but it seems really easy for that to give the whole thing a slapstick feel (When really, being a Thief of Fate should be moderately horrifying). Alternatively, it feels really easy for it to become an amazing murder tool. Which isn't <i>exactly</i> what I'm aiming for, but I suppose wouldn't be the end of the world... <br /> <br /> So, how nasty are dramatic failures in combat in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T16:29:51-07:00","id":932248,"title":"","content":"Tilt the ever-loving shit out of them. Character slips off in the struggle, lands badly, leg-wrack. Etc, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}